# Live-verified 2026-10-04 for the wizard's entry/validation/cancel
# mechanics: "+ Custom" (its real on-screen label - CLAUDE.md's own
# "+ Custom tune" is slightly stale) opens the pattern keyboard (SOUND
# mode: note letters C D E F G A B, an octave/accidental cycle key, z for
# rest); submitting it EMPTY re-shows the same keyboard rather than
# accepting it (an empty/unparseable pattern doesn't advance to the name
# step); BACK at this point aborts the whole wizard, straight back to the
# Tune picker with nothing created.
#
# Actually typing a real pattern needs TOUCH (see
# keyboard_label_touch_entry.seq's header note on this device's touch-only
# typing model - SOUND pattern mode's key layout differs again from both
# the plain label keyboard and VIBE's own digit grid). This sequence uses
# the TestTuneIndex/TestTuneCustomPattern/TestTuneName hooks to create the
# tune directly afterward and confirms it shows up correctly in the Tune
# picker (collapsed with the "(custom)"-equivalent "*" marker, named, and
# linkable to an alarm) rather than re-deriving the wizard's own keyboard
# coordinates.
#
# Keys: TestClearAlarms=10008, TestAlarmIndex=10009, TestAlarmHour=10010,
# TestAlarmMinute=10011, TestAlarmName=10020, TestClearTunes=10040,
# TestTuneIndex=10041, TestTuneName=10042, TestTuneCustomPattern=10043
IMPORT ../common/wipe_and_prep.seq
APPMSG --int 10008=1 10009=0 10010=7 10011=0 --string 10020=Wakeup
SLEEP 1

TAP down
LONGPRESS select
SLEEP 1
TAP down
TAP down
TAP down
TAP down
TAP down
TAP down
SLEEP 1
TAP select
SLEEP 1
# Signal submenu opens on row 0 (Vibration) - one more down reaches Tune.
# An earlier version of this file pressed SELECT here directly, which
# opened the VIBRATION picker instead (and the downs below overshot into
# its own "Custom pattern help" row) - confirmed the hard way via a
# golden-image review.
TAP down
SLEEP 1
TAP select
SLEEP 1
TAP down
TAP down
TAP down
TAP down
TAP down
TAP down
TAP down
SLEEP 1
SCREENSHOT tune_picker_plus_custom_selected
TAP select
SLEEP 1
SCREENSHOT pattern_keyboard_empty

# Submitting empty re-shows the same keyboard rather than accepting it.
TAP select
SLEEP 1
SCREENSHOT pattern_keyboard_still_showing_after_empty_submit

# BACK aborts the whole wizard - back to the Tune picker, nothing created.
TAP back
SLEEP 1
SCREENSHOT tune_picker_unchanged_after_cancel

# Create the tune directly via the test hooks instead of TOUCH-typing it.
# Back out all the way to the main list first (tune picker -> signal ->
# edit menu -> main list is 3 levels, not 2 - confirmed live while
# authoring this) so the sub-windows get rebuilt fresh against the new
# tune on reopen (see common/wipe_and_prep.seq's reload_ui() note).
TAP back
SLEEP 1
TAP back
SLEEP 1
TAP back
SLEEP 1
APPMSG --int 10040=1 10041=0 --string 10042=Chime 10043="C z E z G"
SLEEP 1
LONGPRESS select
SLEEP 1
TAP down
TAP down
TAP down
TAP down
TAP down
TAP down
SLEEP 1
TAP select
SLEEP 1
# Signal submenu opens on row 0 (Vibration) - one more down reaches Tune.
TAP down
SLEEP 1
TAP select
SLEEP 1
SCREENSHOT tune_picker_triple_still_default

# Chime is the one and only saved tune, so it's the first (and only) tune
# row - PATTERN_SELECT_SOUND_TUNES_BASE (SOUND_PRESET_COUNT=7, so base=8)
# + tune index 0 = row 8, i.e. 7 downs from Triple's own row 1.
TAP down
TAP down
TAP down
TAP down
TAP down
TAP down
TAP down
SLEEP 1
SCREENSHOT tune_picker_with_chime_tune
TAP select
SLEEP 1
SCREENSHOT custom_tune_screen_apply_tune_name_delete
TAP select
SLEEP 1
SCREENSHOT signal_menu_tune_chime_applied --mask-rect 70x25+0+203
